    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "JAL\nJapan Airlines\nSAFETY INSTRUCTIONS\n147R\n#M TAKE-OFF AND LANDING\nBAGGAGE\nPlace baggage in the overhead bins or under a seat.\nPlease stow baggage securely.\n83 2\nFASTEN SEAT BELT TIGHT AND LOW Keep seat belt fastened whenever seated.\n*Lint To fasten\nTo tighten\nTo unfasten\nSEAT POSITION\nSet seat back\nand table in\nupright position.\nNO SMOKING\nRefrain from\nsmoking in\nrestrooms or\naisles.\n*E% BRACE POSITIONS",
      "EMERGENCY EXITS\nUPPER DECK\nD D\nDOO\n000000\n000000\n550\n000000000000 00 00\n000000000\n000\n000000\n000\n00\n*HE FOR EVACUATION\nDo not carry any baggage.\nRemove highheeled shoes.\nPut out cigarettes before evacuating.\n# 1#17 DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT",
      "JAL\nJapan Airlines\n147R\nSAFETY INSTRUCTIONS\nInflate when instructed by a crew member.\n2\n3\n4\nLife vest under seat.\n5\n6\n7\n8\n3000\nFor extra inflation blow into\nBybđt3. To Inflate.\npieces.\n57*0580#X5 TO FT THE LIFE VEST TO A CHILD\n2\n3\nPull string to light emergency bea-\ncon.\nPass the straps between\nthe legs and secure\nin front.\n•********Infant life vests provided by crew members.\nB*7X OXYGEN MASK\nOxygen mask will appear automatically when needed.\nPut out your cigarette immediately.\nPULL\nAdults accompanied by small children should secure their own mask first."
    ],
